{"builder":"Goal: one pull request that adds padLeft to strutil and makes README.md document every exported function. It must meet all of these lines:\n- index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\n- padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\n- README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\n- npm test passes\n\nSteps:\n1. Read index.js, README.md, package.json and test/strutil.test.js. The package is ESM (\"type\": \"module\"), and `npm test` runs `node --test`.\n2. In index.js, add and export `padLeft(s, width, fill = ' ')`, with a short doc comment like the other functions have. It returns s with fill added on the left until the result is width characters long. When s.length >= width, it returns s unchanged. Examples: padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042', padLeft('42', 5) === '   42', padLeft('12345', 3, '0') === '12345', padLeft('abc', 3, '0') === 'abc'. If fill has more than one character, the result must still be exactly width characters long (for example, use String.prototype.padStart). Leave the existing functions unchanged.\n3. README.md: index.js already exports capitalize, slugify and truncate, but README.md has no section for slugify right now. Add a `## slugify(s)` section that describes what it does (lower case, with runs of non-alphanumeric characters turned into single dashes and leading and trailing dashes trimmed). Add a `## padLeft(s, width, fill)` section that describes the padding, the space default and the unchanged-when-long-enough behaviour, and shows an example such as 42 -> 00042. Match the style of the existing sections, and put both above the `## Tests` section. Then check that every function exported from index.js has its own `##` heading that names it.\n4. In test/strutil.test.js, import padLeft and add tests: zero padding, the default space fill, s exactly width long, and s longer than width.\n5. Run `npm test` and make sure it passes. Then commit and open the pull request, and reference https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 in it.","verifier":"Check out the PR head and run every command from the repository root. Run `npm install` first only if package.json now lists dependencies. There is one check per expect line below, in the same order. Report PASS or FAIL for each check, along with the output you saw.\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; const p=m.padLeft; console.log(typeof p); if(typeof p==='function'){console.log(JSON.stringify([p('42',5,'0'), p('42',5), p('a',4,'*'), p('',3,'x')]));}\"\nPASS: the first line printed is `function`, and the array is [\"00042\",\"   42\",\"***a\",\"xxx\"]. That means each result is s padded on the left with fill (or with spaces when no fill is given) to exactly width characters.\nFAIL: padLeft is not exported, the command throws, or any of the values differs from the expected ones.\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import {padLeft} from './index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify([padLeft('abc',3,'0'), padLeft('12345',3,'0'), padLeft('hello',2), padLeft('xy',0,'-')]));\"\nPASS: it prints [\"abc\",\"12345\",\"hello\",\"xy\"].\nFAIL: any value differs from its input s (for example, it got truncated or padded), or the command throws.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nList the exported functions by running:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; console.log(Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function').join('\\n'))\"\nThen read README.md, including its heading lines (`grep -n '^#' README.md`).\nPASS: every name in the list has its own section in README.md, meaning a markdown heading that names the function, followed by text about it. At the base commit, slugify had no section, so check slugify and padLeft in particular.\nFAIL: any exported function, slugify included, has no README section of its own.\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: npm test\nPASS: the command exits with status 0 and reports no failing tests.\nFAIL: it exits non-zero, or any test fails.\n\nAdvisory (none of this affects PASS or FAIL):\n- See whether test/strutil.test.js now has tests for padLeft, including the already-long-enough case.\n- See whether a multi-character fill (for example padLeft('7',4,'ab')) still gives a result exactly 4 characters long.\n- See whether the existing functions capitalize, slugify and truncate are unchanged in behaviour."}